cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OQSolv, please cite this software archive and the associated scientific publication when available."
title: "OQSolv: Open Quantum System continuum solvation utilities"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gil Perez"
    given-names: "Gabriel Jose"
    email: "gabrieljose.gilperez@uniupo.it"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gabriel-gil/OQSolv"
abstract: >-
  OQSolv is a Python implementation of Open Quantum System extensions of
  continuum solvation models, including OQS-PCM and OQS-Onsager workflows,
  preprocessing utilities, regression data, and developer/user documentation.
keywords:
  - open quantum systems
  - polarizable continuum model
  - OQS-PCM
  - OQS-Onsager
  - solvation
  - computational chemistry
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-04-30"
